## File Organization Rules

### Directory Structure
- ALWAYS verify the current working directory before creating files
- The project root is `/Users/alejandromedina/dev/FC/workflows/workflows/flowcraft`
- All configuration files (package.json, tsconfig.json, etc.) should be in the project root (flowcraft/)
- Apps go in `apps/` directory
- Packages go in `packages/` directory
- Infrastructure configs go in `infrastructure/` directory
- Documentation files stay in the workspace root (outside flowcraft/)

### File Creation Guidelines
- Before creating any file, check the current directory structure using `list_dir`
- Use `list_dir` to verify the correct location
- Ensure files are created in the appropriate subdirectories
- Follow the established monorepo structure strictly
- NEVER create files in the wrong directory - always verify first
- The workspace structure is: `/Users/alejandromedina/dev/FC/workflows/workflows/` (workspace root)
- The project structure is: `/Users/alejandromedina/dev/FC/workflows/workflows/flowcraft/` (project root)

Remember: Always prioritize user experience, code quality, and system reliability. The goal is to create a platform that makes workflow automation accessible to both technical and non-technical users while maintaining enterprise-grade reliability and scalability. 